### Ask the assistant (IntelliJ HTTP Client). Replace the key with a merchant's API key.
@apiKey = sk_test_replace_me

### 1. A question answered from the documentation (RAG)
POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "message": "What does insufficient_funds mean and what should my customer do?" }

> {% client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.conversationId); %}

### 2. A question that needs the merchant's data (tool calling), continuing the same conversation
POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "message": "Did any of my recent payments fail for that reason?", "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}" }

### 3. Payouts
POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "message": "How much money is waiting to be paid out, and when will I get it?" }

### 4. The assistant is read-only: it explains how to refund instead of doing it
POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "message": "Refund my last payment." }

### 5. Forget a conversation
DELETE http://localhost:8085/api/v1/assistant/conversations/{{conversationId}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
